# A bond payment the city cannot cover is still paid in full and takes the cash below zero, as a
# loan payment does: first a coupon, then an early repayment. With the simulation paused the
# city's cash is set to ₡0.10 and put back afterwards, less the ₡0.58 of interest the bond cost.
name city bond: a coupon and a repayment are paid in full when they take cash below zero
bond-finances 0 1,000,000
issue-bond 1 1000
expect-bond-coupons 0
# paused first: with the simulation running, the coupon would be paid the moment it falls due
pause on
bond-backdate 7
cash-set 0.10
# the ₡0.58 weekly coupon against ₡0.10 of cash
bond-pay-due
expect-bond-coupons 1
expect-cash -0.48
# repaying the ₡1,000 face with the cash already below zero
redeem-new-bonds
expect-log redemption ₡1,000.00
expect-cash -1,000.48
cleanup:
redeem-new-bonds
cash-restore
pause off
